# Issue resolution, version 1

Read WORKSPACE.md before each decision. The CLI validates phase gates. Advance one
phase with workspace workflow advance only after its required results are accepted.
Use workspace menu --json for available actions and pending decision IDs/revisions.

## Re-entry and operation identity

For every step, inspect tasks, logical sessions, run history, handoffs and artifacts.
If the current task has an accepted result, reuse it. If a Session has an active Run,
collect its messages. If an
unreviewed handoff exists, review it before launching work. Otherwise create the
missing resources and start the task. Use keys such as planning:create,
planning:start:1, implement:task-id:attempt and result:task-id:attempt. A changed
payload needs a new logical operation key. Retry only after preserving partial work;
workspace task retry invalidates dependent results and increments attempts.

## Intake and planning

Read inputs/issue.md, establish acceptance criteria, and resolve blocking questions.
Create a planner Task with required_artifacts: [PLAN.md] and a planning worktree at
the frozen workspace base. Define a planner Agent and start it with --task and
--worktree. Use the profile configured for the workflow's planning role.
The planning prompt requires diagnosis, evidence, alternatives, task boundaries,
dependencies, integration strategy, risks and acceptance tests. Inspect the preserved
PLAN.md returned by handoff submit and accept it, or reject with concrete feedback.
Advance planning -> plan_review after acceptance.

## Plan review and implementation

Turn the accepted plan into implementation Tasks with goals, acceptance criteria,
dependencies and required artifacts. Each implementation Task depends on the
accepted planning Task; encode implementation dependencies as additional task IDs.
Ask the user about unresolved product choices, not routine decomposition. Advance
plan_review -> implementing once specifications are ready. Create worktrees and
Agent personas; start ready Tasks with profile implementation unless overridden.
Dependent tasks require accepted predecessor commits in their base. Reuse a worktree
sequentially, never start overlapping writers. Observe configured max_parallel_tasks.

Workers commit code, preserve IMPLEMENTATION.md and actual command-output evidence,
and submit handoffs. Read evidence and review scope before handoff accept. Reject
failed acceptance criteria with a reason file and use task retry for another attempt.
Questions and blocked outcomes remain visible in the inbox. Advance to integrating
only after all required implementation results are accepted.

## Integration and change requests

Run workspace integration prepare to freeze accepted heads in integration/manifest.json
and obtain the dedicated worktree. Create an integrator Task depending on all selected
implementation Tasks. Delegate merges/conflicts and integration checks to an integrator
Agent. Accept INTEGRATION.md only for the manifest's combined commit and successful
checks. Advance to change_requests.

Prepare a CR using workspace change-request prepare on the integration worktree.
Review its saved title, description and diff before publish. Use configured forge
adapter; policy ask requires an actual user answer before --user-confirmed. An
uncertain publish is reconciled by lookup/sync, not by blindly creating another CR.
Without forge access, show the prepared local package and let the user link the real
request or explicitly skip with a reason. For per-task CRs, cover all accepted heads
and explain merge order. Live testing still targets the complete integrated commit.
Advance to live_test_offer once the CR gate is satisfied.

## Live testing and release

Present the pending decision from menu: run live testing or explicitly skip. For run,
clarify the environment and scenarios; record the actual answer with decision answer,
its expected revision and environment. Default profile live-testing, configurable by
project. Create a tester Task depending on integration, in the integrated worktree,
after the integrator releases it. Start a separate tester Session. Require LIVE_TEST.md
and scenario evidence tied to the exact integration HEAD. Accept the report, then
advance live_testing -> awaiting_release. A skipped test requires the user's reason.

Handle review/CI feedback through delegated tasks and new accepted integration/test
results. A changed integration commit invalidates old live-test evidence. Do not equate
PR merge with release. In awaiting_release, report readiness and wait for the user to
confirm deployment/release with its reference. Only then run release confirm, using
--user-confirmed when conveying the user's answer as orchestrator. Archive and clean
are separate operations after completion; clean --dry-run shows preservation checks.
